          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "Not until you know why it fails. A failing assert is either a real bug or a wrong expectation, and loosening it only hides a real bug.\n\n- **Loosening is fine** if the old assert was over-specified, such as an exact float, an ordering that isn't guaranteed, or a timestamp. In that case, tighten it to what the contract actually promises instead of just widening it.\n- **Loosening is not fine** if the code is returning something it shouldn't. The green suite then hides a regression.\n\nTo tell which, check what the assert is meant to guarantee and compare the actual value to the expected one. If you paste the assert and the failure output, I can say which case it is."
        },
